  "facts": [
    "The Hsuehshan Tunnel, 12.942 km long, opened on June 16, 2006, slashing travel time between Taipei and Yilan County from two hours to just thirty minutes.",
    "Construction began in July 1991, spanning 15 years and costing NT$90.6 billion, during which engineers faced fractured rock, massive water inflows, and a TBM buried by a ground collapse.",
    "Today, the tunnel enforces a 90 km/h speed limit, with cameras monitoring tailgaters and lane changers, and a 50‑meter separation rule even during congestion."
